    {
      "text": "who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come, Matt. 3:7 (Luke 3:7). wrath of God abideth on him, John 3:36. heard these sayings, they were full of wrath, Acts 19:28. wrath of God is revealed from heaven, Rom. 1:18. Because the law worketh wrath, Rom. 4:15. we shall be saved from wrath through him, Rom. 5:9. endured … the vessels of wrath, Rom. 9:22. variance, emulations, wrath, Gal. 5:20. we … were by nature the children of wrath, Eph. 2:3. let not the sun go down upon your wrath, Eph. 4:26. because of these things cometh the wrath of God, Eph. 5:6. wrath of God cometh on the children of disobedience, Col. 3:6. Jesus, which delivered us from the wrath to come, 1 Thes. 1:10. wrath is come upon them to the uttermost, 1 Thes. 2:16. God hath not appointed us to wrath, 1 Thes. 5:9. pray … lifting up holy hands, without wrath, 1 Tim. 2:8. he forsook Egypt, not fearing the wrath of the king, Heb. 11:27. let every man be … slow to wrath, James 1:19. wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God, James 1:20. same shall drink of the wine of the wrath of God, Rev. 14:10. cup of the wine of the fierceness of his wrath, Rev. 16:19.",
